.TH MSTREGDUMP "1" "March 2020" "mstflint" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mstdump \- Mellanox mstdump utility, dumps device internal configuration data
.SH SYNOPSIS
mstregdump [\-full] [\-\-i2c_secondary I2C_SECONDARY] [\-\-output_file FILENAME] <device> [i2c\-slave] [\-v[ersion] [\-h[elp]]]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-full\fR
Dump more expanded list of addresses
Note: be careful when using this flag, None safe addresses might be read.
.TP
\fB\-\-i2c_secondary\fR I2C_SECONDARY
I2C secondary [0-127]; it can also be given after the device
.TP
\fB\-\-output_file\fR FILENAME
Write the dump to a file instead of the screen
.TP
\fB\-v\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version info
.TP
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
Print this help message
.IP
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
mstregdump 0b:00.0
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B mstflint(1)
